Negative control for the AC-8 prop-vocabulary gate.

The gate exists because the retired `@upmind/ui` prop API fails SILENTLY: a
`label` on a Badge is not an error, it is an unknown attribute, so it falls
through to the DOM and the badge renders empty. Every count-based assertion
still passes — the element is there, it just says nothing. That is the exact
shape of the defect this story was opened for.

The mutant re-speaks the retired API at one real call site: the impersonation
cue in `SessionSwitcher.vue`, the badge whose emptiness started the audit. It
does not remove the slot children beside it, so the badge still LOOKS right in
the DOM — only the gate can tell. A mutant that blanked the badge would be
caught by the render specs too, and would prove nothing about this gate.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Expected RED (component + module lanes):
  ui-prop-vocabulary.spec.ts  "names every call site still speaking the retired
                                API"
                              -> ["app/components/scope/SessionSwitcher.vue
                                   Badge.label"]

Everything else stays GREEN, including this file's own discrimination cases
("tells an offending call site from a clean one") — they run on synthetic
sources and never read the tree. That asymmetry is the point: only the sweep
over the real tree can see this mutant.

